course: dictionary
lesson: 13886
title: Proper names and special meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of places, and they can also turn into everyday words. Kremlin is one of these. When it has a capital K and «the» in front, as in «the Kremlin», it names one famous place in Moscow. Context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «The Kremlin has red walls and tall towers beside Red Square.» Red walls and towers are clues that this is a place, a fortress. Leo thinks it must be a shop because it sounds like a name, but the walls show it is a big old building.
explain: News writers often use «the Kremlin» to mean the people who run Russia. «The Kremlin said the new rule would start in May.» Here the Kremlin is not a building. It means the Russian government, because a building cannot say things. When you read «the Kremlin said», ask: could a building make a statement?
fact: The Kremlin is an old walled fortress in the centre of Moscow.
fact: The President of Russia has his offices inside the Kremlin.
fact: Its red walls and towers stand beside Red Square.
fact: In the news, «the Kremlin» can mean the Russian government.
fact: The word «kremlin» with a small k means any old Russian walled fortress in the middle of a city.
exercise: «The Kremlin is an old walled fortress in the middle of Moscow.» What is the Kremlin? | A river that runs through Russia | A school for young children | A shop in Moscow | *An old walled fortress in the middle of Moscow
exercise: «The news said the Kremlin has made a new plan.» What does the Kremlin mean here? | A small park in Moscow | A children's playground | *The Russian government | A type of Russian soup
exercise: Mia says a kremlin is any old Russian walled fortress in a city. Which word tells you a kremlin is a building? | Says | Russian | Plan | *Walled
test: «We walked past the red towers of the Kremlin on our trip to Moscow.» Where did they walk? | A zoo in Russia | A busy motorway | A beach by the sea | *Past the old walled fortress in Moscow
test: «The Kremlin said the new rule would start in May.» Who made the rule? | *The Russian government | A teacher at school | A football club | My neighbour next door
exam: Which sentence uses kremlin with a small k, meaning any old walled fortress? | The Kremlin said it would send more soldiers. | We visited the Kremlin and saw the red walls. | The Kremlin is in Moscow, beside Red Square. | *Every old city in the region once had its own kremlin, a walled fortress in the middle.
